          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उतरणे (utarṇe) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from uttarati, \"passes over; alights, descends\" (CDIAL 1770). CDIAL traces the sense from \"crosses over\" to \"lands\" to \"alights\" and so \"descends\"."
